{"id":"0ad3f0a56f9e2f35db00c90e6984294e14b06c0e","axis":"silent","repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector","sha":"0ad3f0a56f9e2f35db00c90e6984294e14b06c0e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".chloggen/mdatagen-exporter-queue-check.yaml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+change_type: enhancement","+component: cmd/mdatagen","+note: \"Generate exporter queue/batch sender defaults from an opt-in `sending_queue` field in metadata.yaml. See the [batching migration RFC](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/blob/main/docs/rfcs/batching-migration.md).\"","+issues: [15963]","+subtext: \"Declaring `sending_queue` is opt-in; an exporter that omits it is unaffected until it explicitly opts in one at a time during Phase 2 of the migration. Set MDATAGEN_SENDING_QUEUE_OPT_OUT=true to generate the standard default for every undeclared exporter while auditing a whole repository.\"","+change_logs: [user]"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Makefile","lines":["@@ -214,6 +214,7 @@ prepare-contrib:"," \t@echo Setting contrib at $(CONTRIB_PATH) to use this core checkout"," \t@$(MAKE) -j4 -C $(CONTRIB_PATH) for-all CMD=\"$(GOCMD) mod edit \\"," \t\t$(addprefix -replace ,$(join $(ALL_MOD_PATHS:%=go.opentelemetry.io/collector%=),$(ALL_MOD_PATHS:%=$(CURDIR)%)))\"","+\t@$(MAKE) -C $(CONTRIB_PATH)/internal/tools tidy"," "," \t@$(MAKE) -j4 -C $(CONTRIB_PATH) gotidy"," \t@$(MAKE) generate-contrib"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"cmd/mdatagen/README.md","lines":["@@ -58,6 +58,93 @@ Below are some more examples that can be used for reference:"," "," You can run `cd cmd/mdatagen && $(GOCMD) install .` to install the `mdatagen` tool in `GOBIN` and then run `mdatagen metadata.yaml` to generate documentation for a specific component or you can run `make generate` to generate documentation for all components."," ","+### Exporter queue/batch sender defaults","+","+Declaring a `sending_queue` field in `metadata.yaml` is **opt-in**: an","+exporter that omits it entirely is treated as not yet audited as part of","+the [batching migration RFC](../../docs/rfcs/batching-migration.md), and","+mdatagen generates no `sending_queue`-related code or documentation for","+it. Exporters opt in to Phase 2 of that migration one at a time by adding","+an explicit `sending_queue` block, even just `support: default`.","+","+The exporter config must declare exactly one named, top-level field with","+type `configoptional.Optional[exporterhelper.QueueBatchConfig]` and the","+`mapstructure:\"sending_queue\"` tag. Nested or squashed queue fields are not","+supported.","+","+```yaml","+sending_queue:","+  support: has_overrides","+  overrides:","+    enabled: true","+    num_consumers: 1","+    batch:","+      enabled: true","+```","+","+#### default","+","+The default setting can be set explicitly:","+","+```yaml","+sending_queue:","+  support: default","+```","+","+> [!NOTE]","+> The default behavior uses the `pkg.exporterhelper.queueBatchEnabled`","+> feature flag to determine the `batch::enabled` value. This value is","+> changing to `true` as documented in the [batching migration RFC](../../docs/rfcs/batching-migration.md).","+","+#### has_overrides","+","+When set to `has_overrides`, overrides are provided in the `overrides`","+field, for example:","+","+```yaml","+sending_queue:","+  support: has_overrides","+  rationale: \"Batching is disabled because ...\"","+  overrides:","+    enabled: true","+    batch:","+      enabled: false","+```","+","+Overrides are considered relative to the post-migration default.  The","+`overrides::enabled` and `overrides::batch::enabled` fields are","+explicitly required. Set `overrides::batch::enabled` to false to","+disable batching before or after the [batching","+migration](../../docs/rfcs/batching-migration.md).","+","+#### omitted","+","+When set to `omitted`, the sending queue is not used in the exporter.","+","+```yaml","+sending_queue:","+  support: omitted","+  rationale: \"The protocol requires special support ...\"","+```","+","+Unlike an undeclared `sending_queue` field, an explicit `support: omitted`","+requires a `rationale` and generates documentation recording that","+decision.","+","+#### Auditing a repository's exporters (opt-out mode)","+","+Set the `MDATAGEN_SENDING_QUEUE_OPT_OUT` environment variable to a truthy","+value (e.g. `MDATAGEN_SENDING_QUEUE_OPT_OUT=true make generate`) to flip the","+undeclared-`sending_queue` default from `omitted` (opt-in, skip","+generation) to `default` (opt-out, generate the standard default for every","+exporter). This is intended for developers doing the Phase 2 audit across","+a whole repository: it materializes generated code and documentation for","+every exporter without first hand-editing every `metadata.yaml`, so","+overrides can be added only where the standard default is wrong. This","+environment variable is temporary; it is expected to be removed once the","+Phase 2 audit completes, at which point the opt-out behavior becomes the","+permanent, hardcoded default.","+"," ### Central configuration file"," "," `mdatagen` supports a repository-level configuration file named `.mdatagen.yaml`."],"additions":87,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"cmd/mdatagen/go.mod","lines":["@@ -51,6 +51,16 @@ require ("," \tgolang.org/x/tools v0.50.0"," )"," ","+require (","+\tgithub.com/cenkalti/backoff/v7 v7.0.0 // indirect","+\tgithub.com/hashicorp/golang-lru/v2 v2.0.7 // indirect","+\tgo.opentelemetry.io/collector/client v1.68.0 // indirect","+\tgo.opentelemetry.io/collector/config/configretry v1.68.0 // indirect","+\tgo.opentelemetry.io/collector/exporter v1.68.0 // indirect","+\tgo.opentelemetry.io/collector/extension v1.68.0 // indirect","+\tgo.opentelemetry.io/collector/extension/xextension v0.162.0 // indirect","+)","+"," require ("," \tgithub.com/Microsoft/go-winio v0.6.2 // indirect"," \tgithub.com/cespare/xxhash/v2 v2.3.0 // indirect","@@ -74,8 +84,10 @@ require ("," \tgo.opentelemetry.io/a